is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence
(CC BY 4.0), not under the MIT licence that covers the source code.

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

You are free to share and adapt this data, including commercially, provided you
give appropriate credit and indicate whether changes were made.

Suggested attribution:

    Round-trip execution cost measurements for tokenized equities on Solana,
    Adnan Husayn, 2026. https://haircut-fi.vercel.app — CC BY 4.0

Why this data is licensed separately: these are timestamped observations of
market state, recorded every fifteen minutes and spanning the transition from
the US market being closed to open. They cannot be reconstructed after the
fact from any public source. MIT is a software licence and fits a dataset
poorly; CC BY is the instrument built for this, and it asks only for credit.

The data is provided as-is, with no warranty as to accuracy or fitness for any
purpose. It is a record of what public APIs returned at a moment in time. It
is not investment advice.
